# Identity resolution

Guardrails: G-09, G-10, G-13, G-14, G-15

## States (G-13)

- Use exactly: MATCHED, PROBABLE, UNRESOLVED, REJECTED. Do not add states or collapse them.
- When the evidence does not settle a case, its state stays UNRESOLVED.
- Fuzzy or similarity matching only generates candidates. It is never proof and never
  produces MATCHED on its own.
- Every resolution records state, method, confidence classification, evidence, and rule version.
- A changed decision creates a new version with an audit record (G-10).

## Separate concepts (G-14)

- Legal entity, economic group, and instrument are resolved independently.
- Never infer an economic group from name similarity alone.

## Instruments (G-15)

- Same borrower does not mean same loan. Different tranches, seniorities, or security types
  are never merged. When continuity is not unambiguous, keep the records separate and UNRESOLVED.

## CIK (G-09)

- CIK stays on BDC and filing records and never becomes a borrower, legal-entity, or
  economic-group identifier.
- Never infer a registrant CIK from an accession-number prefix.
- Phase 2 does not match amendments: every `/A` filing is UNRESOLVED with no target.

```text
BAD : borrower_id = filing.cik
GOOD: borrower identity resolved from disclosed names plus evidence; CIK stays on the filing
```
